  "Question": "A group of children riding on bicycles and tricycles rode past Billy Bob’s house. Billy Bob counted \\(7\\) children and \\(19\\) wheels. How many tricycles were there?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "A bicycle has \\(2\\) wheels, and a tricycle has \\(3\\). Imagine first that all \\(7\\) children are riding bicycles. That would account for\n\\[\n7\\cdot2=14\n\\]\nwheels. Each tricycle contributes exactly one more wheel than a bicycle, so the \\(19-14=5\\) extra wheels mean there are \\(5\\) tricycles.\n\nThis leaves \\(2\\) bicycles, and \\(5\\cdot3+2\\cdot2=19\\), as required. The answer is \\(5\\), choice \\(C\\).",
